--- CODE CONDUCT RULES ---

Python:
  - snake_case: variables, functions, modules
  - PascalCase: classes, model names
  - SCREAMING_SNAKE: constants
  - Views call service functions — no ORM queries inside views
  - All form input validated through Django Form or ModelForm + model clean()
  - No bare except — specific exception types only
  - No raw SQL unless parameterized cursor.execute() is unavoidable

JavaScript:
  - camelCase: variables, functions
  - SCREAMING_SNAKE: constants
  - All fetch() calls live in api.js only — never inline in templates or handlers
  - All loading, error, and empty states handled explicitly
  - Handle loading/error/empty in every async action

General:
  - No comments on obvious logic — comments only for non-obvious business rules,
    workarounds, external API quirks, known limitations with TODO
  - No generic variable names: result, data, temp, item, obj, val
  - Name everything after domain meaning (cart_total not total)
  - No AI-pattern signatures: no "Here is the...", no list-of-steps comments,
    no excessive interface prefixes
  - Max 3 levels of indentation before extracting a function
  - Readable over clever when they conflict